! Oracle anchor, v1.21.2.  ECP: LANL2DZ with an effective core
! potential, against ORCA 6.0.1.
!
! The pair of files _num and _ana differ ONLY in %ecp_method, and
! that is the point: StudDFT implements the ECP integrals twice --
! numerically, by radial-angular quadrature, and analytically, by
! McMurchie-Davidson with Flores-Moreno angular projection.  Two
! implementations of one quantity against one external reference.
!
! The paper reports the analytical route as the less accurate of
! the two (MAD 13.8 against 4.2 uHa) and numerical is the default
! for that reason.  The tolerances below reflect that: they are
! not the same for the two files, because the two routes are not
! equally good, and pretending otherwise would hide a change in
! either.
!
! ECP integrals: analytical
%method  HF
%basis   LANL2DZ
%ecp     LANL2DZ
%ecp_method analytical
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%spherical
%scf_etol 1e-10
%scf_ptol 1e-8
%scf_diis_etol 1e-7
%geom angstrom
H       0.0000000000      0.0000000000      0.0000000000
P       0.0000000000      0.0000000000      1.4200000000
H       1.3505002531      0.0000000000      1.8588041320
H      -0.6752501266      1.1695675270      1.8588041320
*end
